rm a concealed Chow of [W4, W5, W6] later, which could contribute to patterns like Fully Concealed Hand (4 points) and All Chows (2 points). Additionally, maintaining concealed melds is strategically advantageous for maximizing points.\n\nReason: Passing preserves the potential for higher-value concealed patterns and avoids exposing melds prematurely. The risk of losing scoring opportunities by taking an exposed Chi outweighs the immediate benefit of completing a third Chow now.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
