h tile to discard to make room for drawing a W6?\n\nIf I discard T1, then I have W5, W6 (2), W7, T6, T7, B9. Then, if I draw a W6, I can form the pung. Then, the remaining tiles would be W5, W7, T6, T7, B9. Need to form another meld. Maybe T6-T7-T8. But again, need T8.\n\nThis is getting too tangled. Maybe the best move is to discard a tile that is not part of any potential meld. The T1 is a terminal and not part of any chow I can form easily. So discarding T1 might be the best option. That way, I can focus on forming chows in T and W. If I discard T1, the valid action is Play T1.\n\nAlternatively, if I discard T6, which is an extra tile in the meld, to make room for T8. Let's see the unshown tiles: T8 has 3 left, which is a lot. So the chance of drawing T8 is higher. So discarding T6 might be better.\n\nBut if I discard T6, then I have to rely on getting T8. If I discard T1, I can still get T8, but I lose the terminal. It's a trade-off.\n\nAnother consideration: the current hand has a possible pair of W6. If I keep both W6s, and draw another, that's a pung. But I need to discard a different tile to make room for the pung.\n\nSo if I discard T1, I can keep the two W6s and aim for a pung. If I discard a W6, I lose one, making it harder.\n\nSo between discarding T1 or T6.\n\nIf I discard T1, I can still form W5-W6-W7 chow and aim for T8. If I discard T6, I can aim for T8 but lose an extra tile.\n\nGiven that T8 is more available (3 left) compared to W4 (2 left) or W8 (3 left), maybe discarding T6 to get T8 is better. Because forming a chow in T might be easier.\n\nSo I think the best move is to discard T6. Let me check the valid actions: Play T6 is an option. So the answer would be Play T6.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: Discarding T6 allows forming a potential chow in T suit with T7 and T8, which is more feasible given the availability of T8. Keeping W6s could lead to a pung if drawn, but T8 is more abundant.\nReason: Discarding T6 (an extra tile from the existing meld) opens the possibility to complete a T6-T7-T8 chow. With three T8 remaining, this is a high-probability path. The W6s can still form a pung if another is drawn, but T8 availability is better.\nAnswer: Play T6"}
